{
  "title": "iOS UI tests pass without ever leaving the login screen",
  "description": "The iOS UI test job runs `xcodebuild test` with \
`CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO` (both in `.github/workflows/ios.yml` and `make \
ios-test-ui`). Without code signing the app bundle has no entitlements, so \
KeychainHelper's `kSecAttrAccessGroup = \"group.com.ramekin.app\"` operations \
fail: the login POST returns 200 (visible in server logs), but the token is \
never persisted, `AppState.refreshState()` still sees a logged-out API, and \
the app silently stays on the login screen with no error.\n\
\n\
`RecipeFlowTests.testRecipeFlow` still passes because its \"recipe list \
loaded\" check is `app.cells.firstMatch.waitForExistence` — and LoginView is a \
SwiftUI `Form`, whose rows are also `cells`. The test then \"taps the first \
recipe\" (a login form row) and screenshots \"02-RecipeList\" / \
\"03-RecipeDetail\" that are actually the login screen. Verified locally on \
2026-07-12: server logs showed the 200 login and zero subsequent /api/recipes \
requests while the suite passed.\n\
\n\
So the only UI coverage of the recipe list is vacuous, and any regression in \
the logged-in UI is invisible to CI.\n\
\n\
Scope:\n\
- Make login work under the UI test harness. Options: sign simulator test \
builds (needs GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE=YES or Info.plist files for the test \
targets), or make KeychainHelper fall back to no access group when the \
entitlement is missing (simulator/dev only — fail fast in release).\n\
- Fix testRecipeFlow to assert on something only the logged-in UI has (e.g. \
the Recipes navigation bar) instead of `cells.firstMatch`, so it can never \
pass from the login Form again.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "bug",
